cts precipitation. Use a salt other than mine. Do not solve my problem. Then ask me one short question and wait for my answer.", "return_ask": "What does Q use that Ksp does not?", "park_text": "\\( Q_{sp} = [\\mathrm{cation}]^a[\\mathrm{anion}]^b \\) now, after mixing; compare with Ksp.", "status": "approved (instructor, 17 Oct 2026)"}, "conc_found": {"state": "conc_found", "stage": "calculate", "label_when_done": "Concentrations after mixing found", "ask": "Find each ion's concentration after mixing. Type both with their units.", "switch_ask": "Moles stay the same when you mix; the volume becomes the sum of both solutions.", "notebook_prompt": "Show me how to find concentrations after two solutions are mixed. Use numbers other than mine. Do not solve my problem. Then give me one short practice problem and wait for my answer.", "return_ask": "Which volume do you divide by?", "park_text": "c(after) = c(before) × V(own) ÷ V(total).", "status": "approved (instructor, 17 Oct 2026)"}, "Q_found": {"state": "Q_found", "stage": "calculate", "label_when_done": "Qsp found", "ask": "Find Qsp. Type its value.", "switch_ask": "Raise each concentration to its count in the formula, then multiply.", "notebook_prompt": "Show me how to calculate Qsp from concentrations after mixing. Use numbers other than mine. Do not solve my problem. Then give me one short practice problem and wait for my answer.", "return_ask": "Did you keep the exponents?", "park_text": "\\( Q_{sp} = [\\mathrm{cation}]^a[\\mathrm{anion}]^b \\) after mixing.", "status": "approved (instructor, 17 Oct 2026)"}, "verdict": {"state": "verdict", "stage": "inference", "label_when_done": "Verdict given", "ask": "Compare Qsp with Ksp. Does a precipitate form? Pick one.", "switch_ask": "Is Q larger or smaller than Ksp?", "notebook_prompt": "Explain what happens when Q is above, equal to, or below Ksp. Do not solve my problem. Then ask me one short question and wait for my answer.", "return_ask": "Which way does Q above Ksp